    {
      "id": "the-first-part-of-king-henry-the-fourth/sceneI_9.1/p@8629",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "KING.\nBut I have sent for him to answer this;\nAnd for this cause awhile we must neglect\nOur holy purpose to Jerusalem.\nCousin, on Wednesday next our Council we\nWill hold at Windsor, so inform the lords:\nBut come yourself with speed to us again,\nFor more is to be said and to be done\nThan out of anger can be uttered.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
